      <Comment source="O-28, pujar">A cDNA clone was isolated from germinated unpolished |FRAME: TAX-4530 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt;| grains which contain a higher amount of |FRAME: D-SERINE D-serine|. This gene encoded a putative serine racemase gene called serr. This gene was recombinantly expressed in E.coli, the gene product was purified to homogeniety. This enzyme was bifunctional and catalyzed serine racemization and dehydratase activity |CITS: [19249065]|.</Comment>
